   "description": "Worship is the total orientation of the person toward God — expressed in posture, voice, action, and the ordering of the whole life around his worth. The Hebrew vocabulary covers bowing down (shachah) and the service or ministry (abad) that gives God what he is owed; the Greek adds the sense of doing homage. Worship is not merely what happens in a gathered service but the fundamental posture of the creature rightly relating to the Creator: giving God what he is worth, which is everything. It is the outer expression of the inner reality of love, trust, and reverence.",
